    <briefdescription>
<para>DPDK poll-mode server for ultra-high-throughput, low-latency I/O. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The server bypasses the kernel TCP/IP stack entirely. It requires:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>A DPDK-compatible NIC bound to VFIO or UIO.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Huge pages configured on the host (e.g. <computeroutput>vm.nr_hugepages</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Build flag <computeroutput>THEMIS_ENABLE_DPDK</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>When <computeroutput>THEMIS_ENABLE_DPDK</computeroutput> is absent the class compiles without change but <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_d_p_d_k_server_1ad1164f5e9b29cb19bdb391b72fa98c01" kindref="member">start()</ref></computeroutput> returns false and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_d_p_d_k_server_1a735b46d4621ac36bddbeb7336502cc42" kindref="member">lastError()</ref></computeroutput> explains why.</para>
<para>Performance characteristics:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Latency: 1–10 µs end-to-end</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Throughput: up to 100 Gbps on compatible NICs</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CPU model: spinning poll loop (no interrupts, no context switches) </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
